    "silhouette_change": -0.5508210711942824,
    "interpretation": "The silhouette is lower after preprocessing (0.885 -> 0.334). On raw features Monetary (std 8,302 GBP, skewness 21.5) dominates Euclidean distance, so K-means mostly isolates a few extreme spenders (raw cluster sizes [4198, 3, 15, 106]). Such a split of one huge group plus tiny outlier groups can score a high silhouette while saying almost nothing about recency or frequency. After log1p and standardization all three features contribute equally (cluster sizes [1183, 887, 1546, 706]), producing balanced, interpretable segments whose boundaries run through dense regions, which naturally lowers silhouette. Silhouette values are computed in each model's own feature space and are not directly comparable; cross-space scores are reported alongside."
  },
